Subject: [PATCH] wave: validate the A0 FixedPower selector before publication

The matching Gen6 A0 firmware implements FixedPower selectors zero through
four. Other byte values reach the ordinary peer descriptor writer with an
invalid selector and assert. Reject them before storing the request or
submitting a firmware message. Keep the other chip-generation paths and
the existing valid-selector behavior unchanged.

--- a/wireless/driver/linux/core.c
+++ b/wireless/driver/linux/core.c
@@ -5629,9 +5629,17 @@
 _mtlk_core_store_and_send_fixed_pwr_cfg (mtlk_core_t *core, FixedPower_t *fixed_pwr_params)
 {
   wave_radio_t *radio = wave_vap_radio_get(core->vap_handle);
+  mtlk_hw_t *hw = mtlk_vap_get_hw(core->vap_handle);
   MTLK_ASSERT(NULL != radio);
 
+  /* A0 implements selectors 0..4. Other byte values reach its peer
+   * descriptor writer's invalid-selector assertion. Reject them before
+   * either the requested-value cache or the firmware can observe them. */
+  if (mtlk_hw_type_is_gen6(hw) && !mtlk_hw_type_is_gen6_b0(hw) &&
+      fixed_pwr_params->changeType > 4)
+    return MTLK_ERR_PARAMS;
+
   if (MTLK_ERR_OK != WAVE_RADIO_PDB_SET_BINARY(radio, PARAM_DB_RADIO_FIXED_PWR, fixed_pwr_params, sizeof(*fixed_pwr_params)))
     ELOG_V("Failed to store Fixed TX management power parameters");
 
   return _mtlk_core_send_fixed_pwr_cfg(core, fixed_pwr_params);
